	(NULL, 'Machine Learning Engineer', 'Park Controls and Communications Private Limited', NULL, 'Full-time', 'Bangalore', NULL, NULL, '0-2 years', '["C/C++", "Python", "Machine Learning", "Data Processing", "Feature Engineering", "Model Training", "C++/Qt", "LLMs", "Prompt Engineering", "Telemetry Data Processing"]', 'We are seeking an AI / Machine Learning Engineer with knowledge in C/C++ to develop and integrate AI predictive analytics and anomaly detection solutions for real-time and offline telemetry data processing. The role involves building Machine Learning models, implementing AI/LLM-based capabilities such as report generation and intelligent analysis, and integrating these solutions into C++/Qt applications. The engineer will work with telemetry data from shared memory, UDP streams, and files to detect anomalies, generate insights, and support decision-making.', NULL, '2026-07-10 07:08:46.012223+00', true, '2026-06-10 07:08:46.012223+00', '2026-07-18 08:38:16.285984+00', 'Technology Solutions', 'Entry Level', NULL, NULL, 'open', '2026-06-10 07:08:46.012223+00', '2026-07-10 07:08:46.012223+00', '["Bachelor''s or Master''s degree in Computer Science, AI/ML, ECE, Data Science, or a related field", "Knowledge in C/C++", "Programming skills in Python for ML model development", "Knowledge of data processing, feature engineering, and model training", "Strong problem-solving and analytical mindset", "Ability to collaborate with multi-disciplinary teams and communicate technical concepts clearly", "Experience in documenting processes and findings effectively", "0-2 years of experience preferably in Aerospace and Defence sectors"]', '["Develop and integrate ML-based anomaly detection and predictive analytics into a C++/Qt application", "Work on data-driven failure prediction for real-time telemetry systems", "Implement techniques for handling missing data and improving model accuracy", "Develop solutions for handling real-time data from shared memory and UDP and offline data from CSV and logs", "Optimize models for low-latency inference in real-time environments", "Work with software engineers to integrate ML models into C++/Qt-based systems", "Use Large Language Models for text summarization, report generation, and information extraction", "Apply prompt engineering and work with LLM APIs"]', NULL, 2, 0, 0, NULL, 'Machine Learning Engineer', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Aerospace & Defence - Electronics Manufacturing', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '04afe0f4-4ce6-4c92-a625-972928e9bcd3', NULL, NULL),
